{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1541482-cindersoul-kith","id":1541482,"title":"Cindersoul Kith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-09-03T13:42:18-07:00","id":1541482,"title":"Cindersoul Kith","content":"I swear this is the last one. Comments/critiques as ever. Many thanks!<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:48px\"><span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Vivaldi\"><span style=\"color:#76923c\">Cindersoul</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><span style=\"color:#76923c\"><i>My fairy godmother turned out worse than my step-mother.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\">Many Cindersouls began life in Arcadia as Firehearts or similar, starting as conflagrations. However, they were then forgotten about by their creators after their fuel was used up. Yet others were deliberately made to be drudges or moldable statues. They are not a common kith, but find it relatively easy to escape back to reality due to their inherent powers and their jailors' general lack of interest in them.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Beast:</i> Clearly someone started out designing a dragon. Equally clearly they gave up in disgust half way through.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Darkling:</i> They're an indistinct creature made of slowly flowing white dust and ash.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Elemental:</i> Ash and glowing cinders float freely from her glassy hair and limbs.<br /> <br /> <i>Fairest:</i> Her exquisitely fine features seem almost drawn in charcoal, with a sweeping mass of shifting black hair.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Grimm:</i> A young beauty covered in soot, and wearing the rags of once fine garments.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Ogre:</i> He cuts a brutish figure appearing to have been roughly carved from coal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Wizened:</i> He has a stunted posture, and his limbs seem like they could fall apart, were they not stabilized by glowing metal and glass at the joints.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><b>Kith Blessing:</b> The Cindersoul gains an exceptional success with three successes when using Survival to withstand any deprivations that don\u2019t equate to actual Tilts or Conditions.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Cambria\"><span style=\"font-family:Times\"><i>Ashes Ashes:</i> Cindersouls take only Bashing damage from fire. Once per Scene, he can spend one point of Glamour to briefly become less solid for one turn per point of Wyrd. In this state he downgrades all damage (so is briefly immune to fire) and can crawl through any barrier with an opening. However, he moves at half speed and cannot carry objects. Any contact with water instantly ends the effect.</span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8297-greg-davis","user":"Greg Davis","date":". 09-04-2024, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8297-greg-davis","name":"Greg Davis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}